      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "QUEEN OF THINKING (7) goes on top again after missing by a long neck at Ballina when sent out favourite, and that was only her second race start. She does have to see out 1900m for the first time, but the race-fit profile, weight relief and sharp improvement from debut make her the one to beat. SHE LOVES ME (6) is the main danger, with a second and third from three runs this campaign and enough evidence around this distance to be a genuine winning threat despite coming back from 2224m. WASAI (5) gets the blinkers applied after a run of honest placings and has the profile of a horse who can sharpen up with the gear change. BLOOD RED (1) has placed at his past two and backs up quickly, though his long maiden record keeps him more in the each-way bracket. MISSION WISE (2) was better when sent forward last time at Ballina. Fitter again and is drawn to lead them up once more over the longer trip.",
